                <pb facs="0835" n="715" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg715"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4450: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-12T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 12, 1922—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 12—11:01
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>259. Li Yuan-hung, temporarily assuming duties of President, at Palace yesterday
                    but lives in private residence for the present. Mandate dated the 11th names W.
                    W. Yen Acting Premier. Yen countersigned mandate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
